You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Particle Network (`bg-particles`)

Drifting particles that link with lines when close and gently flee the cursor — the classic network hero.

## What it should do
Build a particle network on canvas: particle count = area × density; particles drift with damping and wrap around edges, are pushed away within 120px of the pointer; draw lines between pairs closer than `link` with alpha (1 − d/link)·.35.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **canvas**.
- No runtime dependencies (CSS only).
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/bg-particles.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** aria-hidden; static frame under reduced motion.
- **Performance:** Density-scaled particle count; O(n²) links capped by density — keep it to hero areas.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

